            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Development of the Rotative Engine</strong><br>\nWatt continued to innovate by developing engines that could turn a shaft and thus drive machinery. His introduction of the double-acting engine and the sun-and-planet gear made the steam engine more versatile, powering a wide range of industrial processes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Watt's Patents and Legal Battles</strong><br>\nWatt patented his inventions to protect his designs, but he was often involved in legal battles over his patents. These disputes underscored the competitive and lucrative nature of technological innovation during the era.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Scientific Studies and Innovations</strong><br>\nBeyond steam engines, Watt investigated the composition of water, experimented with gas lighting, and developed the concept of horsepower. He even coined the term \"horsepower\" and proposed the unit of power known as the watt.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
